// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// machinedpens — refill compatibility model  ·  PASTABLE ERD
//
// This file IS the paste. Copy with:
//   pbcopy < .notes/data-model-erd-clean.eraser
//
// Rendered OK in app.eraser.io on 2026-08-12 — every construct here is
// verified legal (see .notes/eraser-integration-findings.md, Q4).
//
// VISUAL ENCODING, ported from data-model-erd.md 2026-08-15. This file had
//   drifted PLAIN while the annotated copy carried icons and colours — which
//   made the file that calls itself "the paste" the least readable of the six.
//   Colour marks the section: blue = the pen side · green = refills ·
//   purple = refill styles · orange = the assertion corpus (the moat) ·
//   red = style_adapter · gray = the collection.
//   THREE ENTITIES ARE DELIBERATELY LEFT PLAIN — also_known_as, part_needed
//   and part_fitted — and they are exactly the LINK/ALIAS tables. Unadorned
//   reads as "this is a join, not a thing". Keep it that way.
// ⚠️ THIS IS STILL THE IMPLEMENTATION REFERENCE, NOT A REVIEW ARTIFACT: it
//   carries internal names and all 42 house-style timestamp rows. For a team
//   review use the buyer-facing views — and prefer the three SCOPED ones,
//   because 20 entities on one canvas is the hairball lexicon §4 names, and
//   the recorded fix is SPLITTING, not ordering.
//
// Reflects decisions through SITTING 3 (complete 2026-08-12), plus 4.1-4.4b.
//   4.1  `fit_report` + `fit_check.evidence` (replaced `verified bool`)
//   4.1b nothing renders until approved — fit_report has NO buyer read path
//   4.3  `source` split three ways: claimed_by / made_by / citation_*
//   4.4  the verdict is DERIVED (demotion #9); `fit_check.disputed_note` is
//        the staff override for maker copy that is a typo or a copy-paste
//   4.4b NO disputed_note on refill_dimension — a bad number is DELETED.
//        `claimed_by` added there instead, and a geometry negative fires only
//        on an unconflicted `feature` or a `staff` row. Displayed measurement
//        is DERIVED (demotion #10).
//   4.5  TWO CORPORA — catalog broad (scraper stages, human promotes) vs
//        fit_check narrow and deep, seeded NEGATIVES-FIRST. Zero fit rows is
//        not empty: it renders the PRIOR (refill_style + observance), a 4th
//        display state. Coverage is DERIVED (demotion #11). No new columns.
// SITTING 4 IS COMPLETE. RATIFICATION SWEEP COMPLETE 2026-08-13:
//   S1 the slot_option -> part merge · S2 3.2b's tip_option override ·
//   S3 4.3's source split. All three were already applied; the sweep bought
//   certainty, not columns. ZERO soft decisions remain in the model.
//   C1  `rebrand` — the branded SKU points at the OEM part it actually is
//       (Retro 51 REF5P -> Schmidt P8126). Closes lexicon §2.7. Carries the
//       4.3 attribution shape because the mapping is CONTESTED in the wild.
//       The verdict rule gains a step -1: expand the fit_check set to
//       R + R's rebrand partners, ONE HOP, labelled "via Schmidt P8126".
//       ⚠️ SAME PART, NEVER SAME STYLE — style-mates belong to refill_style.
//   C2  VOCABULARY STORAGE — a table when members arrive at RUNTIME or carry
//       data; a TS `as const` when the set is closed at compile time and a
//       member is nothing but its own name. All ~20 curated vocabularies here
//       are the second kind. `material` is the only one of the first, and it
//       is INHERITED — the committed `materials` table (scraper.ts:191),
//       declared here only so product_variant's FK resolves. `mechanisms` and
//       `product_types` are scraper staging, NOT ours to model.
//       product_variant.material string null -> material_id (was free text:
//       no fixed list AND no shared list). `finish` stays free text, flagged.
//   C3  the committed `mechanisms` / `product_types` tables are NOT corrected
//       and NOT used. Both are interned from scraped strings — "click" is a
//       QUOTE from Autmog's page, not a modelling claim. Promoting it is a
//       SPLIT (-> ratchet + top_button) and it is UNDERDETERMINED, so a human
//       does it. Confirms 4.5's "cheap per row, still a human".
//   C4a `claimed_by` gains a FIFTH value: maker|retailer|community|owner|staff.
//       On refill_dimension claimed_by is the ONLY trust signal (4.4b kept
//       `evidence` off), so merging "measured it" with "retyped it" would
//       destroy it. Fisher PR: Unsharpen 90x4.8 vs Penstore 89x5.8.
//   5.3a DIRECTION CHANGE — field-log dropped, web-only, no app integration.
//       A saved config is A PEN YOU OWN (finish + pen tip + what's loaded),
//       not a wishlist and not an inventory. collection_item gains user_id;
//       `user` is INHERITED (the committed users table, PR #63).
//       It is also the fit_report entry point: 4.1 wants a report to name a
//       tip_option, and a saved config already does.
//   5.2 THE REFILL GRAIN — `refill` IS A MODEL. tip_size and colour were
//       single-valued columns on a row a Sarasa fills with 3 sizes x 20
//       colours: a column whose CARDINALITY CONTRADICTS ITS ROW'S GRAIN.
//       Both moved to a new `refill_variant`, the refill-side twin of
//       product_variant (same job: surface differences that must never
//       duplicate the assertion corpus). Five of the six FKs into `refill`
//       already wanted the model; only collection_item.installed_refill_id
//       leaned SKU-ward — ANSWERED by 5.3b(i) below, (c) BOTH.
//       COLOUR SPLIT IN TWO — colour_name free text (the long tail, the
//       maker's own word) + colour_family enum (black|blue|blue_black|red|
//       green|other, the browse facet). The bucket cannot be derived from the
//       name, so it is curated. NINTH axis-mix. Starts coarse and grows.
//       CLOSES C1's OPEN 5.2: a rebrand is MODEL -> MODEL.
//   5.3b(i) INSTALLED REFILL — (c) BOTH. collection_item keeps
//       installed_refill_id (the MODEL, what every read path uses) and gains
//       installed_refill_variant_id (THE EXACT ONE, optional). Coarse +
//       precise, the shape already run four times. R-A killed the cold-start
//       case for model-only: Pentel, uni and Pilot each publish a COMPLETE
//       size x colour matrix, and the code printed on the refill in your pen
//       (LR7, UMR-85N, LP3RF-12S4) already names the size. Exact-only was
//       refused because NOTHING forces refill_variant to be populated while
//       fit_check forces `refill` to exist.
//       THE TWO CANNOT DISAGREE — refill_variant needs UNIQUE (id, refill_id);
//       collection_item takes a two-column FK (installed_refill_variant_id,
//       installed_refill_id) -> refill_variant (id, refill_id), plus
//       CHECK (installed_refill_variant_id IS NULL OR installed_refill_id IS
//       NOT NULL). NOT match full — that would forbid the model-only case.
//       KNOCK-ON RENAME: variant_id -> product_variant_id. Two "variants" on
//       one row (pen finish vs refill option) is naming-law trap 3.
//       blue_black added to colour_family — R-A found it first-class at all
//       three makers, which pays off the flagged R-D claim.
//   5.3b(ii) COLLECTION RESIDUE — (a) NOTHING MORE, AND LESS ENTRY. No
//       nickname, no note, NO COLUMNS. The row already stores zero specs, so
//       they read through to the catalog; what is new is that the four FKs
//       arrive PRE-FILLED from the stock config. RULE: fill what the catalog
//       makes unambiguous, ASK ONLY WHERE IT BRANCHES (one tip_option, fill
//       it; more than one, ask once). WRITTEN AT SAVE TIME, not resolved on
//       read — otherwise a curator's catalog edit would silently change what
//       is loaded in every saved pen (4.4's mutable-vs-owned line), a report
//       would carry a value the owner never saw (4.1), and null would mean
//       both "empty" and "stock". NO note column: pairing prose belongs in
//       fit_report.note where a curator can promote it.
//   5.4 MULTIPLES — SEPARATE ROWS, ALWAYS. Never a quantity: it cannot say
//       which refill is in the second one, cannot be the subject of a report
//       (4.1), and counting what you own is the inventory shape 5.3a left.
//       BVG corrected the REASON — what separates two copies is usually a
//       FINISH or a SMALL PART, not the refill. Finish was already covered;
//       parts were not, so + `part_fitted` (collection_item x part), the
//       20th entity. R-F confirmed the case and the catalog needed NOTHING:
//       TT sells the Bolt Action Back Piece alone in Ti/Cu/Bronze/Zirc,
//       "mixed and matched between pens" but "select the correct diameter
//       (Standard, Slim, or Thick)" — which IS part.family_id, 3.2 (a').
//       CURATION RULE: parts that change how it LOOKS are the owner's choice
//       and go here; parts that change how it FITS are dictated by the refill
//       and part_needed already holds them. part.kind is the test.
//       NO tip_variant — R-F found NO maker selling a tip alone in an alloy
//       (TT machines tip and body together; Fellhoelter's spare kit is an
//       o-ring, a spring and a refill). Logged as the TENTH axis-mix,
//       AVOIDED. Revisit if a maker ever sells tips by alloy.
//       NO nickname — the parts list closed the gap that argued for it.
//   5.5 WHAT'S LOADED IS A FIELD, NOT A LOG. "Log from day one" was
//       field-log's OWN premise and field-log is dropped. The log's one
//       durable use — what was loaded WHEN SOMEONE SAID IT FITS — is
//       fit_report, append-only already (4.1). A pen you own is MUTABLE
//       state (4.4's line), which is what updated_at is for. A log later is
//       an append-only child + a twelfth demotion, no backfill.
//       RE-CENTRED: this layer is PEN + PARTS first, refill second.
//   5.6a THE COMPLETENESS GATE — you cannot own what the catalog does not
//       fully have. NEEDS NO COLUMN: collection_item's required FKs already
//       say it (maker + product + finish + tip, and the tip declares a
//       refill_style). Same bar 4.5 set from the other end. No `published`
//       flag: staging is tmp_*, so being in a curated table IS promotion.
//       A pen we lack routes to a SUBMISSION — fit_report's pattern one
//       corpus over. Out of scope, not modelled, shape recorded.
// Entity count: 20 entities / 37 edges. The open_5_carry_log SHELL IS GONE
//   — 5.5 answered it (a field, not a log), so there is nothing left to
//   scaffold. Zero shells remain in the model.
//   VALIDATED 2026-08-14: every relationship endpoint in all five .eraser
//   files resolves to a declared entity and an existing column.
//
// HOUSE STYLE applied 2026-08-12 (naming thread, ratified by BVG):
//   inherited from the COMMITTED schema — packages/database/src/schema/
//   and docs/database-schema/{makers,mechanisms,materials,product-types}.md
//     · id bigint pk          (was `string`; FKs follow to stay coherent)
//     · created_at / updated_at timestamptz on every entity
//     · slug text unique      on canonical entities only
//     · maker.root_url text unique
//   Non-id `string` columns are deliberately UNTOUCHED — converting them
//   to `text` was not part of the ratified patch.
//   Rationale + the collisions we did NOT inherit: .notes/vocabulary-lexicon.md §5
//
// NAMING: `tip_option` > `nose_option` was proposed and REJECTED (BVG,
//   2026-08-12) — "tip is still better". Closed, not parked. Five OTHER
//   renames landed under the naming law; see .notes/vocabulary-lexicon.md §0.1.
//   Buyer-facing labels live in .notes/data-model-erd-public*.eraser, which
//   are views, never the schema of record.
//
// Field-level provenance lives elsewhere, deliberately:
//   .notes/data-model-answers.md   — SOURCE OF TRUTH, has a RESUME HERE block
//   .notes/data-model-erd.md       — the annotated ERD, comments carry decision numbers
//
// ERASER DOC URL: ____________________________________________
//   ^ paste it here once the canonical diagram exists, so future
//     sittings update that diagram in place instead of minting a new one.
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

title machinedpens — refill compatibility model
notation crows-feet
typeface clean
styleMode plain

// ── CATALOG ─────────────────────────────────────────

maker [icon: factory] {
  id bigint pk
  slug text unique
  name string
  root_url text unique
  created_at timestamptz
  updated_at timestamptz
}

product_family [icon: layers] {
  id bigint pk
  maker_id bigint
  slug text unique
  name string
  created_at timestamptz
  updated_at timestamptz
}

product [icon: pen-tool, color: blue] {
  id bigint pk
  maker_id bigint
  family_id bigint null
  slug text unique
  name string
  advance_mechanism enum
  actuator enum
  bore_class enum
  bore_mm decimal null
  axial_adjust enum
  accepts_length_min_mm decimal null
  accepts_length_max_mm decimal null
  radial_retention enum
  handedness enum
  created_at timestamptz
  updated_at timestamptz
}

tip_option [icon: git-merge, color: blue] {
  id bigint pk
  product_id bigint
  refill_style_id bigint
  name string
  toleranced_for_refill_id bigint null
  axial_adjust enum null
  accepts_length_min_mm decimal null
  accepts_length_max_mm decimal null
  ships_with_refill_id bigint null
  created_at timestamptz
  updated_at timestamptz
}

material [icon: box] {
  id bigint pk
  slug text unique
  name string
  created_at timestamptz
  updated_at timestamptz
}

product_variant [icon: droplet, color: blue] {
  id bigint pk
  product_id bigint
  finisher_maker_id bigint null
  material_id bigint null
  finish string null
  name string null
  one_off bool
  created_at timestamptz
  updated_at timestamptz
}

// ── REFILL STYLES ─────────────────────────────────────────

refill_style [icon: crosshair, color: purple] {
  id bigint pk
  slug text unique
  name string
  standard string null
  observance enum
  variance_note text null
  created_at timestamptz
  updated_at timestamptz
}

also_known_as {
  id bigint pk
  refill_style_id bigint
  alias string
  created_at timestamptz
  updated_at timestamptz
}

// ── REFILLS ─────────────────────────────────────────

refill [icon: edit-3, color: green] {
  id bigint pk
  slug text unique
  brand string
  model string
  refill_style_id bigint
  medium enum
  rear_topology enum
  form enum
  created_at timestamptz
  updated_at timestamptz
}

refill_variant [icon: layers, color: green] {
  id bigint pk
  refill_id bigint
  tip_size decimal null
  colour_name text null
  colour_family enum null
  created_at timestamptz
  updated_at timestamptz
}

rebrand [icon: copy, color: green] {
  id bigint pk
  refill_id bigint
  oem_refill_id bigint
  claimed_by enum
  citation_url text null
  citation_note text null
  created_at timestamptz
  updated_at timestamptz
}

refill_dimension [icon: maximize-2] {
  id bigint pk
  refill_id bigint
  feature string
  value decimal
  unit string
  claimed_by enum
  citation_url text null
  citation_note text null
  created_at timestamptz
  updated_at timestamptz
}

// ── ASSERTIONS ──────────────────────────────────────

fit_check [icon: link, color: orange] {
  id bigint pk
  refill_id bigint
  tip_option_id bigint null
  refill_style_id bigint null
  polarity enum
  reason text null
  fit_quality enum null
  trim_mm decimal null
  trim_reference string null
  trim_necessity enum
  functional_warning bool
  claimed_by enum
  evidence enum
  citation_url text null
  citation_note text null
  disputed_note text null
  created_at timestamptz
  updated_at timestamptz
}

fit_report [icon: message-square, color: orange] {
  id bigint pk
  refill_id bigint
  tip_option_id bigint
  fits bool
  note text null
  review_state enum
  fit_id bigint null
  created_at timestamptz
  updated_at timestamptz
}

part [icon: tool] {
  id bigint pk
  maker_id bigint null
  family_id bigint null
  slug text unique
  kind enum
  name string
  made_by enum
  created_at timestamptz
  updated_at timestamptz
}

part_needed {
  fit_id bigint
  part_id bigint
  sourcing enum
  necessity enum
  created_at timestamptz
  updated_at timestamptz
}

style_adapter [icon: shuffle, color: red] {
  id bigint pk
  part_id bigint
  from_style_id bigint
  to_style_id bigint
  result_quality enum null
  scope_tip_option_id bigint null
  created_at timestamptz
  updated_at timestamptz
}

// ── COLLECTION ──────────────────────────────────────

user [icon: user] {
  id bigint pk
  clerk_id text unique
  created_at timestamptz
  updated_at timestamptz
}

collection_item [icon: package, color: gray] {
  id bigint pk
  user_id bigint
  product_variant_id bigint
  tip_option_id bigint
  installed_refill_id bigint null
  installed_refill_variant_id bigint null
  created_at timestamptz
  updated_at timestamptz
}

part_fitted {
  collection_item_id bigint
  part_id bigint
  created_at timestamptz
  updated_at timestamptz
}

// ── SITTING 4 COMPLETE — 4.1 / 4.1b / 4.3 / 4.4 / 4.4b / 4.5 ────
//   NO residual OPENs. The one that stood here — no `claimed_by` value fit
//     a RETAIL listing reprinting a spec (Penstore) — was CLOSED by C4a on
//     2026-08-13 with a fifth value, `retailer`. Marker was stale; cleared
//     2026-08-14.
//   CLOSED by C4b — ships_with_refill_id MOVED from product to tip_option.
//     The refill in the box belongs to the CONFIGURATION you bought, and a
//     fit is tip-scoped. Third application of F3'.
//
// ── RATIFICATION SWEEP — DONE 2026-08-13, shell removed ─────────
//   S1 slot_option -> part merge      RATIFIED
//   S2 3.2b tip_option override       RATIFIED
//   S3 4.3 source split               RATIFIED
//   No columns added or removed. The `// SOFT` markers are gone.


// ── RELATIONSHIPS ───────────────────────────────────

product.maker_id > maker.id
product.family_id > product_family.id
tip_option.ships_with_refill_id > refill.id
product_family.maker_id > maker.id

tip_option.product_id > product.id
tip_option.refill_style_id > refill_style.id
tip_option.toleranced_for_refill_id > refill.id

product_variant.product_id > product.id
product_variant.finisher_maker_id > maker.id
product_variant.material_id > material.id

also_known_as.refill_style_id > refill_style.id

refill.refill_style_id > refill_style.id
refill_variant.refill_id > refill.id
refill_dimension.refill_id > refill.id
rebrand.refill_id > refill.id
rebrand.oem_refill_id > refill.id

fit_check.refill_id > refill.id
fit_check.tip_option_id > tip_option.id
fit_check.refill_style_id > refill_style.id

fit_report.refill_id > refill.id
fit_report.tip_option_id > tip_option.id
fit_report.fit_id > fit_check.id

part_needed.fit_id > fit_check.id
part_needed.part_id > part.id

part.maker_id > maker.id
part.family_id > product_family.id

style_adapter.part_id > part.id
style_adapter.from_style_id > refill_style.id
style_adapter.to_style_id > refill_style.id
style_adapter.scope_tip_option_id > tip_option.id

collection_item.user_id > user.id
collection_item.product_variant_id > product_variant.id
collection_item.tip_option_id > tip_option.id
collection_item.installed_refill_id > refill.id
collection_item.installed_refill_variant_id > refill_variant.id

part_fitted.collection_item_id > collection_item.id
part_fitted.part_id > part.id
